    "To whom it may concern,\r\rIt is my great pleasure to inform you that International Nuclear Safety School (INSS), established within Korea Institute of Nuclear Safety (KINS), starts recruiting new students of the \"KINS-KAIST International Nuclear and Radiation Safety Masterquot;s Degree Program.\"\r\rThis program was jointly designed and developed by KINS together with Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology (KAIST), internationally well known for excellent education and research achievements in science and technology.\r\rThe main purpose of the Masterquot;s Degree Program is to cultivate nuclear and radiation safety leaders through training and education of high-caliber young professionals from individual countries, and to consequently promote the global safety harmonization.\r\rIn December of 2023, this program had its 14th graduates of 6 students from 6 different countries in Asia and Africa. Another 7 students from 7 countries (15th Batch) were enrolled as of August 28, 2023 and are studying nuclear and radiation safety as the class of 2023 of the said program.\r\rThe program for 2024 will start on September 2, 2024 and submission of required documents by the prospective applicants should be made by April 3, 2024. Now I would like to have your kind attention and interest in this program, and cordially request you to encourage your staff members to apply for this program. Because a full scholarship will be awarded to each individual student who is admitted, this program would be a great opportunity for the staff of your institution to get a masterquot;s degree abroad.\r\rYour persuasive encouragement to your staff would be highly appreciated. I would like to extend my great appreciation for your time and effort on this matter in advance.\r\rI look forward to receiving your positive response.\t\t\t\t\t                                                                                                                                                           \r\rYours sincerely,\r\rYoung Eal Lee, Ph.D.\r\rDirector\rInternational Nuclear Safety School\rKorea Institute of Nuclear Safety": 1,
    "To whom it may concern,\r\rIt is my great pleasure to inform you that International Nuclear Safety School (INSS), established within Korea Institute of Nuclear Safety (KINS), starts recruiting new students of the \"KINS-KAIST International Nuclear and Radiation Safety Masterquot;s Degree Program\". \r\rThis program was jointly designed and developed by KINS together with Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology (KAIST), internationally well known for excellent education and research achievements in science and technology.\r\rThe main purpose of the Masterquot;s Degree Program is to cultivate nuclear and radiation safety leaders through training and education of high-caliber young professionals from individual countries, and to consequently promote the global safety harmonization. \r\rIn December of 2022, this program had its 13th graduates of 7 students from 6 different countries in Asia and Africa. Another 6 students from 6 countries were enrolled as of August 29, 2022 and are studying nuclear and radiation safety as the class of 2022 of the said program.\r\rThe program for 2023 will start on August 28, 2023 and submission of required documents by the prospective applicants should be made by March 22, 2023. Now I would like to have your kind attention and interest in this program, and cordially request you to encourage your staff members to apply for this program. Because a full scholarship will be awarded to each individual student who is admitted, this program would be a great opportunity for the staff of your institution to get a masterquot;s degree abroad. \r\rYour persuasive encouragement to your staff would be highly appreciated. I would like to extend my great appreciation for your time and effort on this matter in advance.\r\rI look forward to receiving your positive response.\t\t\t\t\t                                                                                                                                                           \r\t                                                                                                                                                           \rYours sincerely,\r\rYoung Eal Lee, Ph.D.\r\rDirector \rInternational Nuclear Safety School\rKorea Institute of Nuclear Safety": 1,
